// The builtin foreign functions, in bytecode order. An entry's position is the
// index CALL_FOREIGN_INDEXED encodes, so the compiler (names), the disassembler
// (names) and the runtime (function pointers) all expand this one list:
//   MARMOT_BUILTIN(name, argument kinds, return kind)
// Removing or reordering an entry renumbers the ones after it and needs an
// MbcFormatVersion bump; appending does not.
MARMOT_BUILTIN(MIDORI_FFI_Print, MakeFFIArgKinds(FFIArgumentKind::CString), FFIReturnKind::RawValue)
MARMOT_BUILTIN(MIDORI_FFI_PrintError, MakeFFIArgKinds(FFIArgumentKind::CString), FFIReturnKind::RawValue)
